> **Bootstrap note**: The dates above are a starting window from the setup wizard (season length × today). At INTAKE (your first conversation) the mentor confirms or changes them with you, along with domain states, "why this season", exit criteria, and locked slots. You don't fill the `<angle-bracket>` placeholders by hand; talk it through with the mentor instead (FIRST_PRINCIPLES P2).

A **season** is a fixed-duration arc (typically 90 days) with explicit exit criteria per active domain. It bounds ambition, forces choices about what's Active vs Silent right now, and creates a natural archive boundary. Without seasons the system sprawls.

---

## Domain States

Every domain in your `mentors/` folder has exactly one state this season:

- **Active** — gets a weekly mentor consultation, gets time on the calendar, gets archived at season end.
- **Seeding** — gets reconnaissance / intel updates, may get a session or two, but is not on the main weekly cadence yet. Becomes Active in a future season or stays Seeding indefinitely.
- **Silent** — not getting attention this season. Folder exists, files are preserved, no mentor agent spawned, no time budget allocated. Reactivated in a future season if you want.

| Domain | State | Why this season | Exit criterion |
|---|---|---|---|
| <domain> | Active | <one line> | <observable, time-bounded> |
| <domain> | Seeding | <one line> | (none for this season — graduates to Active later) |
| <domain> | Silent | <one line> | (none — sleeping) |

> The point of distinguishing **Seeding** from **Active** is honesty: most people have more interests than they can do real work in. Seeding domains get curiosity, not commitments.

